<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Faesŭlae</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fēs-</span></b> ), ārum,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Etruria</i>, now <i>Fiesole</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Cat.
				3, 6, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 22, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sall. C.
				24, 2</span></i>.—Also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Faesŭla</span></b> , ae, <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			479</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Faesŭlānus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fēs-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Faesulae</i>, <i>Faesulan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 2, 6, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coloni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mur. 24, 49</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Faesŭlā-nus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a Faesulan</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Sall. C. 60, 6</span></i>.</div>
